1
00:00:09,550 --> 00:00:10,740
I'm sorry.

2
00:00:12,130 --> 00:00:13,040
Who are you?

3
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:16,730
The sorcerer who erected
the barrier here.

4
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:19,250
This spot has been chosen

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,890
for people to kill each other in.

6
00:00:22,660 --> 00:00:26,030
Unfortunately,
there's no real honor in it.

7
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:28,240
Kill each other?

8
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:33,050
Could you not do that in
my neighborhood, please?

9
00:00:35,820 --> 00:00:37,820
You're funny.

10
00:00:38,510 --> 00:00:42,070
There's an old execution
site not far from here.

11
00:00:42,070 --> 00:00:44,240
That serves as the center of the barrier.

12
00:00:44,690 --> 00:00:47,030
It covers a five- or six-kilometer radius.

13
00:00:47,710 --> 00:00:51,020
I went through great pains
to create this barrier,

14
00:00:51,020 --> 00:00:54,050
so I can't impose restrictions
that are too unreasonable.

15
00:00:54,610 --> 00:00:59,770
Those of you who were inside the barrier
from the start have the right to leave it.

16
00:01:00,740 --> 00:01:02,330
Just once.

17
00:01:02,930 --> 00:01:06,730
If you wish, you could wake
up outside the barrier.

18
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:10,010
Would you like to?

19
00:01:10,550 --> 00:01:12,840
Wake up?

20
00:01:14,470 --> 00:01:16,220
Is this a dream?

21
00:01:16,220 --> 00:01:18,880
You're in the space between
dreams and reality.

22
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:20,290
It's a curse.

23
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:26,810
Be careful.

24
00:01:26,810 --> 00:01:28,260
Take it slowly.

25
00:01:28,740 --> 00:01:31,910
The hasty ones are already outside.

26
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:00,830
Oh, right.

27
00:02:00,830 --> 00:02:02,760
I nearly forgot to mention it.

28
00:02:04,230 --> 00:02:07,510
Thank you for being friends with my son.

29
00:02:06,250 --> 00:02:07,300
Sasaki!

30
00:02:08,450 --> 00:02:09,490
Sasaki!

31
00:02:10,050 --> 00:02:11,260
Sasaki!

32
00:02:11,650 --> 00:02:12,840
Sasaki!

33
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:16,720
Iguchi!

34
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:19,940
I'm so glad to see someone I know.

35
00:02:20,320 --> 00:02:22,370
My legs hurt...

36
00:02:20,320 --> 00:02:22,370
My glasses are missing...

37
00:02:23,050 --> 00:02:24,810
Where are we?

38
00:02:25,270 --> 00:02:28,580
Somewhere between Kotodai
and Hirose Street.

39
00:02:28,580 --> 00:02:30,030
More importantly, look.

40
00:02:30,370 --> 00:02:31,630
What's your opinion on that?

41
00:02:32,130 --> 00:02:33,700
As an occult club member?

42
00:02:34,540 --> 00:02:36,980
On that?

43
00:02:35,340 --> 00:02:40,510
November 1, 06:02, Sendai Colony

44
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:43,470
Can I talk about a dream?

45
00:02:44,290 --> 00:02:45,720
Everyone's had it.

46
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:47,720
There was a guy with long
hair and a kasaya, right?

47
00:02:48,290 --> 00:02:51,760
Then did he say something
about his son to you, too?

48
00:02:51,760 --> 00:02:54,430
Oh? No, first time hearing about that.

49
00:02:58,710 --> 00:02:59,950
Itadori?

50
00:02:59,950 --> 00:03:02,940
Episode 54
Tokyo No. 1 Colony, Part 1

51
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:14,170
JUJUTSU KAISEN

52
00:03:37,430 --> 00:03:41,600
JUJUTSU KAISEN
The Culling Game Part 1

53
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:34,880
For real?

54
00:04:35,230 --> 00:04:37,420
Gojo-san got sealed?

55
00:04:37,420 --> 00:04:38,870
For real.

56
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:43,390
Damn!

57
00:04:43,390 --> 00:04:45,700
Also, sorry to mention this as an aside,

58
00:04:45,700 --> 00:04:47,260
but the principal's dead, too.

59
00:04:51,900 --> 00:04:53,500
Panda-senpai?

60
00:04:53,500 --> 00:04:56,940
Sorry for not telling you, but it's true.

61
00:04:57,530 --> 00:04:59,470
It's all right, Itadori.

62
00:04:59,470 --> 00:05:01,070
He didn't die in Shibuya.

63
00:05:01,070 --> 00:05:03,460
He fought with the higher-ups after that.

64
00:05:04,010 --> 00:05:06,430
That doesn't make it any better.

65
00:05:06,430 --> 00:05:08,950
The principal was your...

66
00:05:08,950 --> 00:05:11,930
I'm including that in "it's all right."

67
00:05:11,930 --> 00:05:13,080
Thanks, though.

68
00:05:13,650 --> 00:05:17,810
If you say so, then there's
nothing more for us to add.

69
00:05:17,810 --> 00:05:18,710
Yeah.

70
00:05:19,390 --> 00:05:23,380
Still, that's everyone who's
been good to me all at once...

71
00:05:23,380 --> 00:05:24,840
I haven't been this bummed out

72
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:28,340
since I watched Yakul get shot
in the ass with an arrow.

73
00:05:28,340 --> 00:05:30,850
What a nice life you've lived.

74
00:05:30,850 --> 00:05:35,110
All right. I'll help you all
stop this Culling Game.

75
00:05:37,460 --> 00:05:39,480
Don't get me wrong, though.

76
00:05:39,950 --> 00:05:42,280
I'm not doing this out of sympathy.

77
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:44,190
We're cutting a deal.

78
00:05:44,190 --> 00:05:45,700
Got me?

79
00:05:45,700 --> 00:05:50,370
Once we clean up this Culling Game,
it's your turn to help me.

80
00:05:50,370 --> 00:05:55,010
You're trying to get in on the revisions
to the Jujutsu Regulations, right?

81
00:05:55,010 --> 00:05:58,370
Now that the existence of
curses has gone public,

82
00:05:58,370 --> 00:06:01,370
there's sure to be some kind of revision,

83
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:04,180
but what exactly are you hoping for?

84
00:06:05,200 --> 00:06:08,720
Whatever it is, I doubt it'll
be that hard to secure.

85
00:06:08,720 --> 00:06:09,800
Huh?!

86
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:13,680
What would you know about it,
Sea Urchin Head?! Huh?!

87
00:06:13,990 --> 00:06:17,060
I'm the head of the Zen'in Clan.

88
00:06:14,730 --> 00:06:17,060
Screw it,
I'll use it where I can.

89
00:06:20,030 --> 00:06:21,690
Oh, yeah?

90
00:06:23,780 --> 00:06:26,740
Wait, wait, wait, wait, for real?!

91
00:06:26,740 --> 00:06:27,950
I'm sorry for the other two,

92
00:06:27,950 --> 00:06:30,150
but that's the most shocking
thing I've learned today!

93
00:06:30,150 --> 00:06:32,560
If I got the backing of one
of the big three families,

94
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:35,080
I could easily influence the
revisions to the regulations.

95
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:36,630
The only problem would come later,

96
00:06:36,630 --> 00:06:38,300
in trying to keep the Zen'in Clan from

97
00:06:38,300 --> 00:06:40,770
getting involved in managing
the fight club.

98
00:06:41,920 --> 00:06:43,310
Sea Urchin Head!

99
00:06:43,310 --> 00:06:44,520
It's Fushiguro.

100
00:06:44,520 --> 00:06:45,680
Fushiguro-kun!

101
00:06:50,070 --> 00:06:51,820
Let's be friends?

102
00:06:51,820 --> 00:06:52,750
Sure.

103
00:06:53,020 --> 00:06:55,560
The Next Day,
The Zen'in Clan Is Exterminated

104
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:59,610
Good. That just leaves deciding
who's heading to which Colony.

105
00:06:59,610 --> 00:07:01,210
Yuta went to Miyagi, right?

106
00:07:01,210 --> 00:07:05,020
Ding-dong, ding-dong, ding-dong,
ding-dong, ding-dong, ding-dong!

107
00:07:05,020 --> 00:07:10,190
A Player has added a new
Rule to the Culling Game!

108
00:07:10,190 --> 00:07:13,990
Rule 9: Players shall be able to view the
following information on other players:

109
00:07:12,830 --> 00:07:13,660
8: Players who do not show a
change in points within 19 days of
joining or acquiring points
shall be stripped of their technique.

110
00:07:13,660 --> 00:07:20,840
9: Players shall be able to view the
following information on other players:
name, points, number of
rules added, current Colony.

111
00:07:13,990 --> 00:07:20,340
name, points, number of
rules added, current colony.

112
00:07:21,110 --> 00:07:22,680
I am Kogane!

113
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:25,840
A liaison between Players
and the Culling Game!

114
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:28,580
Did that thing just change
personality midway through?

115
00:07:28,580 --> 00:07:31,760
The first part was an announcement
from the Culling Game!

116
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:37,630
Now I'm speaking as the personal liaison
attached to the Player Itadori Yuji!

117
00:07:39,010 --> 00:07:42,050
Tengen-sama did mention
something about that.

118
00:07:42,050 --> 00:07:43,810
Wait, this still isn't right!

119
00:07:43,810 --> 00:07:47,190
Why would Itadori be counted
as a Player already?

120
00:07:47,190 --> 00:07:50,790
Aside from those Kenjaku gave cursed
techniques or cursed objects,

121
00:07:50,790 --> 00:07:54,290
the only Players should be
those who have entered a Colony!

122
00:07:55,430 --> 00:07:59,090
One type was people whom I had absorb
cursed objects like Yuji Itadori did...

123
00:07:57,790 --> 00:07:59,810
The cursed objects that I distributed
are what's left of the sorcerers

124
00:07:59,810 --> 00:08:02,120
I've been secretly making
pacts for a thousand years.

125
00:08:00,060 --> 00:08:03,210
Of course, I forged my pacts with
more than just sorcerers...

126
00:08:03,210 --> 00:08:05,690
He's actually a human who really existed,

127
00:08:03,210 --> 00:08:08,130
He's actually a human who really existed,
though it was over a thousand years ago.

128
00:08:05,690 --> 00:08:08,130
though it was over a thousand years ago.

129
00:08:08,130 --> 00:08:09,280
Sukuna.

130
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:10,370
Sukuna?

131
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:10,390
Sukuna?

132
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:12,770
I think Sukuna was one of the sorcerers

133
00:08:12,770 --> 00:08:15,670
who forged a pact with Kenjaku
and became a cursed object.

134
00:08:16,250 --> 00:08:19,750
Is participation in the Culling Game
included in their pact, then?

135
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:21,850
That's still strange, though.

136
00:08:22,260 --> 00:08:24,850
You swallowed Sukuna's finger
of your own free will.

137
00:08:24,850 --> 00:08:26,030
I witnessed it.

138
00:08:29,860 --> 00:08:31,240
We'll save that for later.

139
00:08:31,720 --> 00:08:35,840
Itadori, could you have Kogane pull up
the Players' information right now?

140
00:08:37,310 --> 00:08:39,500
Kogane, can you?

141
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:40,650
Sure can!

142
00:08:42,170 --> 00:08:44,170
Ta-da!

143
00:08:45,740 --> 00:08:47,250
This guy.

144
00:08:47,640 --> 00:08:49,960
So this guy originally had 200 points?

145
00:08:50,910 --> 00:08:53,430
I wonder what he was hoping
for by adding a rule.

146
00:08:53,430 --> 00:08:57,480
At the very least,
he's killed 40 people, right?

147
00:08:57,480 --> 00:09:00,060
So it's not going to be a
very nice reason, yeah?

148
00:09:00,060 --> 00:09:01,620
Still, this means

149
00:09:01,620 --> 00:09:05,680
we might be able to progress through the
Culling Game without killing anyone.

150
00:09:06,180 --> 00:09:10,600
Kogane, can you show a list of just
the players with 100 points or more?

151
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:14,740
I'm attached to Itadori Yuji, so...

152
00:09:14,740 --> 00:09:16,360
Oh, it's fine.

153
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:18,240
Do what he asked.

154
00:09:18,240 --> 00:09:20,240
Searching

155
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:23,140
Unless someone who got caught
up in this like Tsumiki did

156
00:09:23,140 --> 00:09:25,810
is in a rush to escape
the barrier, then...

157
00:09:25,810 --> 00:09:27,940
The past sorcerers who have incarnated

158
00:09:27,940 --> 00:09:31,100
also just forged pacts with Kenjaku
for their own reasons,

159
00:09:31,100 --> 00:09:34,170
so they're not necessarily
motivated to do this.

160
00:09:34,520 --> 00:09:38,520
If there's anyone else with an excess
of points like Kashimo...

161
00:09:38,520 --> 00:09:39,960
Right!

162
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:43,910
People who have over 100 points and
no intention of adding a rule!

163
00:09:43,910 --> 00:09:45,270
We can lean on them...

164
00:09:45,270 --> 00:09:48,650
...and make them add a rule to let
Tsumiki escape the Culling Game!

165
00:09:48,980 --> 00:09:49,980
Here you are.

166
00:09:49,990 --> 00:09:52,140
Searching

167
00:09:52,140 --> 00:09:53,360
Hajime Kashimo

168
00:09:52,140 --> 00:09:53,360
Points

169
00:09:52,140 --> 00:09:53,360
Rule Added

170
00:09:52,140 --> 00:09:53,360
Current Colony: Tokyo No. 2

171
00:09:52,140 --> 00:09:53,360
Hiromi Higuruma

172
00:09:52,140 --> 00:09:53,360
Points

173
00:09:52,140 --> 00:09:53,360
Rules Added

174
00:09:52,140 --> 00:09:53,360
Current Colony: Tokyo No. 1

175
00:09:52,160 --> 00:09:53,360
There's another one!

176
00:09:53,710 --> 00:09:54,650
Yeah!

177
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:57,710
First, we'll have to take advantage
of the obstacle Rule 8 poses.

178
00:09:57,710 --> 00:09:58,360
Huh?

179
00:09:58,630 --> 00:10:01,200
What was Rule 8 again?

180
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:04,710
8: Players who do not show a
change in points within 19 days

181
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:04,710
of joining or acquiring points
shall be stripped of their technique.

182
00:10:01,520 --> 00:10:04,710
Players who do not show a change
in points within 19 days

183
00:10:04,710 --> 00:10:20,850
Day

184
00:10:04,710 --> 00:10:06,600
shall be stripped of their technique.

185
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:08,480
It's the Rule that leads to death.

186
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:11,070
So we add a Rule that says,

187
00:10:11,070 --> 00:10:14,060
"It is possible for Players to
transfer points among each other."

188
00:10:14,640 --> 00:10:17,370
That way, if they keep passing
points between each other,

189
00:10:17,370 --> 00:10:20,220
they can avoid being stripped
of their techniques and dying.

190
00:10:21,150 --> 00:10:22,840
Then, if possible, we add one more.

191
00:10:22,850 --> 00:10:28,270
"Players may expend
points to leave the Culling Game."

192
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:28,260
We add a Rule like, "Players may expend
points to leave the Culling Game."

193
00:10:28,260 --> 00:10:32,650
Wouldn't that conflict with the Rule
about the continuation of the game?

194
00:10:32,650 --> 00:10:34,400
I think it would, too.

195
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:37,880
But we might be able to get around
that by adding a condition

196
00:10:37,880 --> 00:10:40,770
like dragging a non-Player into the
Culling Game to take their place.

197
00:10:40,770 --> 00:10:42,510
True.

198
00:10:42,510 --> 00:10:44,880
Would Kogane be making the call on that?

199
00:10:44,880 --> 00:10:48,030
Either way, we know what
we need to do now.

200
00:10:48,030 --> 00:10:48,920
Yeah.

201
00:10:48,920 --> 00:10:53,010
Angel

202
00:10:49,580 --> 00:10:53,010
While we're searching for the Angel
to break the Prison Realm's seal,

203
00:10:53,990 --> 00:10:55,770
we'll pursue Hajime Kashimo

204
00:10:56,750 --> 00:10:58,010
and Hiromi Higuruma,

205
00:10:59,010 --> 00:11:00,070
and hunt them down.

206
00:10:59,010 --> 00:11:00,640
Persuade Players with 100 Points
and No Intention of Adding a Rule

207
00:10:59,220 --> 00:11:00,640
Hunt Down Hajime Kashimo

208
00:10:59,220 --> 00:11:00,640
Hunt Down Hiromi Higuruma

209
00:11:03,130 --> 00:11:05,970
Yeah, there's seriously no "Angel" on here.

210
00:11:06,340 --> 00:11:08,220
That probably isn't her real name.

211
00:11:08,220 --> 00:11:10,120
Just like you're not listed as Sukuna.

212
00:11:11,720 --> 00:11:14,490
Tengen-sama said she was
in eastern Tokyo...

213
00:11:14,490 --> 00:11:16,900
That would be Colony No. 2, then.

214
00:11:17,530 --> 00:11:19,400
You guys know what she looks like?

215
00:11:20,110 --> 00:11:21,910
Apparently, we'll know when see her.

216
00:11:21,910 --> 00:11:23,970
Is that gonna work out?

217
00:11:24,850 --> 00:11:26,160
Well, whatever.

218
00:11:26,160 --> 00:11:28,170
Panda and I will take Tokyo No. 2.

219
00:11:28,170 --> 00:11:30,830
Fushiguro-kyun and Itadori can take No. 1.

220
00:11:30,830 --> 00:11:32,490
Kirara, stand by outside the barriers.

221
00:11:32,490 --> 00:11:33,620
Huh?

222
00:11:33,620 --> 00:11:34,710
Sound good?

223
00:11:35,090 --> 00:11:36,180
What's your reasoning?

224
00:11:36,180 --> 00:11:38,500
Just going by points,
this Kashimo's the strongest one,

225
00:11:38,500 --> 00:11:40,790
so it makes sense for me to take him.

226
00:11:40,790 --> 00:11:42,930
I'm being excluded?

227
00:11:42,930 --> 00:11:46,430
You've got a keen nose, Panda,
so focus on finding the Angel.

228
00:11:47,270 --> 00:11:49,720
The fact that we haven't
already heard from Okkotsu

229
00:11:49,720 --> 00:11:52,450
means we probably can't use cell
phones inside the barriers.

230
00:11:52,450 --> 00:11:55,910
So we'll want someone to keep tabs
on what's going on outside them.

231
00:11:55,910 --> 00:11:57,280
Fine.

232
00:11:57,280 --> 00:11:58,710
Wait.

233
00:11:58,710 --> 00:12:01,280
It might be best for me and
Fushiguro to be split up.

234
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:02,080
Sukuna is—

235
00:12:02,080 --> 00:12:02,950
Shut up.

236
00:12:03,340 --> 00:12:04,700
"Shut up"?!

237
00:12:04,700 --> 00:12:07,950
Our three senpai can't
change their roles.

238
00:12:07,950 --> 00:12:09,350
So quit being selfish.

239
00:12:09,350 --> 00:12:10,460
Selfish?!

240
00:12:10,800 --> 00:12:12,940
I'm just worrying about you here!

241
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:15,720
Are you going to say that every time?

242
00:12:15,720 --> 00:12:18,290
What a pain. Such a waste of time.

243
00:12:18,290 --> 00:12:19,530
Huh?!

244
00:12:19,530 --> 00:12:20,790
Don't fight.

245
00:12:20,790 --> 00:12:31,520
November 11th 12:00 Tokyo
(Remaining Time Until Tsumiki
Must Enter the Culling Game:
7 Days 12 Hours)

246
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:24,610
Hey, I'm Kogane!

247
00:12:24,610 --> 00:12:30,460
Inside this barrier is the Culling Game,
where Players fight to the death!

248
00:12:30,460 --> 00:12:34,190
Once you step inside,
you, too, become a Player!

249
00:12:34,190 --> 00:12:37,700
Are you still willing to enter?!

250
00:12:37,700 --> 00:12:38,320
Yeah!

251
00:12:38,320 --> 00:12:38,940
Yeah.

252
00:12:38,940 --> 00:12:40,280
No issues here.

253
00:12:43,660 --> 00:12:45,990
JUJUTSU KAISEN

254
00:12:43,820 --> 00:12:45,990
Hey, Amai!

255
00:12:48,010 --> 00:12:50,580
I keep waiting for your signal!

256
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:54,760
Uh, well, I hear you,

257
00:12:54,760 --> 00:12:57,340
but there's nothing I can
do if no one's showing up.

258
00:12:57,340 --> 00:12:58,110
Huh?

259
00:12:59,190 --> 00:13:02,300
Are you mouthing off to me now?

260
00:13:03,260 --> 00:13:06,010
No! Look, I'm sorry!

261
00:13:06,010 --> 00:13:07,350
Please forgive me!

262
00:13:08,270 --> 00:13:10,110
If you get too uppity,

263
00:13:12,060 --> 00:13:13,770
I'll run you over.

264
00:13:14,880 --> 00:13:17,510
We need to be wary of the past
sorcerers who incarnated.

265
00:13:17,510 --> 00:13:19,270
My thoughts, too.

266
00:13:19,820 --> 00:13:22,620
But explain it to me
again, Fushiguro-kun.

267
00:13:23,540 --> 00:13:26,020
Some of them are from
a thousand years ago.

268
00:13:26,020 --> 00:13:29,820
Yet the value of a life was way different
even a hundred or two hundred years ago.

269
00:13:29,820 --> 00:13:31,490
Plus, they're sorcerers.

270
00:13:31,490 --> 00:13:33,510
Fighting and death are common for them.

271
00:13:33,510 --> 00:13:34,970
Some may want to die fighting.

272
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:38,480
That might even be why they
forged a pact with Kenjaku.

273
00:13:39,150 --> 00:13:42,280
There's a strong chance that Higuruma
and Kashimo are past sorcerers.

274
00:13:42,820 --> 00:13:44,880
Don't expect a proper negotiation.

275
00:13:44,880 --> 00:13:47,890
Then the other aggressive ones are
going to be cursed spirits, huh?

276
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:49,610
Especially at night.

277
00:13:50,230 --> 00:13:54,010
If they're a modern day sorcerer
dragged into this like Tsumiki,

278
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:57,150
they actually might be open
to exchanging information.

279
00:13:59,050 --> 00:14:00,980
Hey, I'm Kogane!

280
00:14:01,360 --> 00:14:06,950
Inside this barrier is the Culling Game,
where Players fight to the death!

281
00:14:06,950 --> 00:14:10,290
Once you step inside,
you, too, become a Player!

282
00:14:10,290 --> 00:14:12,990
Are you still willing to enter?!

283
00:14:12,990 --> 00:14:15,410
Yeah, no issues here.

284
00:14:17,070 --> 00:14:20,370
Megumi Fushiguro has
joined the Culling Game.

285
00:14:20,370 --> 00:14:22,260
Would you like to see the Rules?

286
00:14:22,260 --> 00:14:24,500
No need. I'm fine.

287
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:24,960
Boo.

288
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:24,960
Boo...

289
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:26,030
Itadori.

290
00:14:26,030 --> 00:14:26,780
Huh?

291
00:14:26,780 --> 00:14:29,120
First, we gather information on Higuruma.

292
00:14:29,690 --> 00:14:30,620
Let's go.

293
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:31,520
Yeah!

294
00:14:37,130 --> 00:14:38,350
Fushiguro's gone?!

295
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:43,220
When a Player enters one of
the Culling Game's barriers,

296
00:14:43,220 --> 00:14:47,650
they're randomly teleported to one
of nine designated locations.

297
00:14:48,060 --> 00:14:50,360
It was a rule of the barriers not included

298
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:52,830
in the general rules of the Culling Game.

299
00:14:52,830 --> 00:14:55,450
But they were waiting in
those nine locations...

300
00:14:55,450 --> 00:14:56,670
Here's one!

301
00:14:57,010 --> 00:15:01,590
Players who targeted those disoriented
by this unmentioned phenomenon.

302
00:15:10,850 --> 00:15:12,550
Newbie-hunters.

303
00:15:14,130 --> 00:15:16,490
He's tough!

304
00:15:16,490 --> 00:15:18,850
This would have turned
most into mincemeat.

305
00:15:18,850 --> 00:15:20,600
But he's still kicking.

306
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:22,230
He's no ordinary person.

307
00:15:31,440 --> 00:15:34,370
Darling, let's meet up.

308
00:15:37,710 --> 00:15:39,820
She fell easily.

309
00:15:39,820 --> 00:15:41,930
I need to ask her about Higuruma.

310
00:15:41,930 --> 00:15:44,200
Then I have to find Fushiguro.

311
00:15:44,720 --> 00:15:45,870
What the hell?!

312
00:15:46,770 --> 00:15:49,090
What did you do to my woman?!

313
00:15:49,620 --> 00:15:51,510
Guess I can just ask him.

314
00:15:51,510 --> 00:15:53,890
Haba-san flew in.

315
00:15:53,890 --> 00:15:55,930
Was Hanyu-san taken out?

316
00:15:55,930 --> 00:15:58,680
I've seen him before...

317
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:01,130
Itadori?!

318
00:16:01,130 --> 00:16:04,870
Ow! That hurts!

319
00:16:04,870 --> 00:16:07,770
Why are you doing this?!

320
00:16:07,770 --> 00:16:09,850
You're the one who attacked me.

321
00:16:10,150 --> 00:16:11,090
Damn it!

322
00:16:11,090 --> 00:16:13,490
I didn't expect us to
get separated that way.

323
00:16:13,750 --> 00:16:14,690
Well?

324
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:17,960
Nue can't find him, either.

325
00:16:17,960 --> 00:16:20,980
This Colony must be much
larger than Shibuya.

326
00:16:20,980 --> 00:16:23,190
We're probably over two kilometers apart.

327
00:16:23,810 --> 00:16:25,870
But we both know where to head.

328
00:16:26,800 --> 00:16:29,140
Do you know a sorcerer named Higuruma?

329
00:16:29,680 --> 00:16:33,620
Men think they can just beat women
into listening to them, don't they?

330
00:16:33,620 --> 00:16:34,670
Answer me!

331
00:16:34,670 --> 00:16:36,590
Yes. I'm sorry.

332
00:16:36,930 --> 00:16:39,260
By Higuruma, you mean that guy, right?

333
00:16:39,260 --> 00:16:40,780
The one with 100 points?

334
00:16:41,410 --> 00:16:42,990
Do you know where he is?

335
00:16:45,750 --> 00:16:48,600
I see. So that's how it is.

336
00:17:01,440 --> 00:17:03,070
Damn brat!

337
00:17:03,070 --> 00:17:05,260
What physical prowess!

338
00:17:11,980 --> 00:17:14,890
I thought I'd be in trouble with him
constantly holding higher ground,

339
00:17:14,890 --> 00:17:17,830
but that propeller's his
only means of attack.

340
00:17:37,940 --> 00:17:40,370
He keeps coming in close
to try to kill me.

341
00:17:40,370 --> 00:17:42,120
I'll fight him indoors!

342
00:17:56,220 --> 00:17:58,460
I'll turn you into a smoothie!

343
00:18:00,570 --> 00:18:03,530
He's turned his head toward me!

344
00:18:05,680 --> 00:18:07,580
That earlier airplane woman

345
00:18:07,580 --> 00:18:10,240
was sturdy enough to smash
through buildings with me,

346
00:18:10,240 --> 00:18:12,240
but she fell from such
a simple thrown object.

347
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:14,960
Their hair is the core
of their technique,

348
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:17,830
so they're probably less sturdy the
further away from their hair you get.

349
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:19,560
Because of a pact?

350
00:18:19,560 --> 00:18:23,030
But no matter how tough it may be,
it's still their head.

351
00:18:23,030 --> 00:18:25,040
As long as I can attack it,

352
00:18:25,040 --> 00:18:26,420
I can crack it open!

353
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:42,780
Broke your fist, did ya?
You just lost this battle!

354
00:18:51,580 --> 00:18:54,600
I didn't break anything. Ow.

355
00:18:54,600 --> 00:18:57,020
I don't mind telling you,

356
00:18:57,020 --> 00:18:59,610
but I want you to do me a favor in return.

357
00:19:01,330 --> 00:19:02,690
Spit it out.

358
00:19:02,690 --> 00:19:05,320
Say it, pl...?

359
00:19:05,320 --> 00:19:07,360
Tell me, pl...?

360
00:19:06,820 --> 00:19:07,830
Say it.

361
00:19:08,890 --> 00:19:09,940
Fine.

362
00:19:11,670 --> 00:19:13,620
Become my knight?

363
00:19:13,620 --> 00:19:15,080
Sure. That's fine.

364
00:19:17,260 --> 00:19:19,740
Am I that much of a bore?

365
00:19:19,740 --> 00:19:21,310
I just don't have time.

366
00:19:21,310 --> 00:19:22,540
Hurry it up.

367
00:19:22,540 --> 00:19:23,730
Walk in front.

368
00:19:23,730 --> 00:19:25,640
Do you even get it?!

369
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:29,890
My knight is supposed to
protect me with his life!

370
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:33,270
I will if you're telling me the truth.

371
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:37,710
Hey, wake up.

372
00:19:37,710 --> 00:19:40,860
I want to ask you about a
sorcerer named Higuruma.

373
00:19:42,310 --> 00:19:44,220
I-Itadori.

374
00:19:45,880 --> 00:19:47,530
I know him.

375
00:19:48,180 --> 00:19:50,280
That Higuruma guy.

376
00:19:51,190 --> 00:19:54,660
You know what will happen
if you're lying, right?

377
00:19:55,520 --> 00:19:57,420
I'm not like Itadori.

378
00:19:57,420 --> 00:19:59,830
I'm willing to earn those
100 points on my own.

379
00:20:00,430 --> 00:20:02,810
Split Ahead

380
00:20:00,430 --> 00:20:02,420
Stop calling me "you."

381
00:20:02,790 --> 00:20:04,300
My name is Remi.

382
00:20:04,840 --> 00:20:06,210
It's been a long time.

383
00:20:06,210 --> 00:20:07,390
Do you remember me?

384
00:20:08,430 --> 00:20:09,140
Who are you?

385
00:20:09,580 --> 00:20:11,710
How does he know my name?

386
00:20:12,220 --> 00:20:13,440
Oh, sorry.

387
00:20:13,440 --> 00:20:15,960
I guess it was just me
who knew about you.

388
00:20:15,960 --> 00:20:17,910
You were famous, you know.

389
00:20:18,310 --> 00:20:19,770
The Tiger of West Middle School.

390
00:20:20,010 --> 00:20:22,660
Oh! You're from my hometown!

391
00:20:22,660 --> 00:20:27,160
Split Ahead

392
00:20:23,900 --> 00:20:27,220
What, you're not a
sorcerer from the past?

393
00:20:27,530 --> 00:20:31,550
Huh? Do I look that far behind the times?

394
00:20:31,840 --> 00:20:34,280
What's your reason for taking
the initiative to fight, then?

395
00:20:34,830 --> 00:20:36,160
Listen, you.

396
00:20:36,520 --> 00:20:41,070
Average people who weren't Players
got let out of the Colony,

397
00:20:41,600 --> 00:20:44,810
but us Players who were in
the Colony from the start

398
00:20:44,810 --> 00:20:48,890
have had to participate in the
Culling Game for twelve days already!

399
00:20:48,890 --> 00:21:09,660
Split Ahead

400
00:20:49,260 --> 00:20:52,290
I'm not doing this because I want to!

401
00:20:52,290 --> 00:20:54,250
It's kill or be killed!

402
00:20:55,790 --> 00:20:58,670
You'll get killed while you're trying
to find your reason to fight.

403
00:20:59,170 --> 00:21:01,720
Anyone can figure that out
after twelve days here.

404
00:21:02,450 --> 00:21:05,480
I've seen plenty of people drown
in their power during that time.

405
00:21:06,120 --> 00:21:09,670
So stop trying to differentiate between
them as past or present sorcerers.

406
00:21:09,990 --> 00:21:12,350
So the past sorcerers have inspired

407
00:21:12,350 --> 00:21:14,910
even the modern-day sorcerers
to go into battle mode.

408
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:17,660
I might have given Itadori
bad advice, then.

409
00:21:18,120 --> 00:21:20,810
Are you sure? You were allies, right?

410
00:21:21,250 --> 00:21:22,050
With those two?

411
00:21:22,540 --> 00:21:24,770
I was just their gofer.

412
00:21:24,770 --> 00:21:26,820
They would have killed me at some point.

413
00:21:26,820 --> 00:21:27,460
Wait.

414
00:21:28,850 --> 00:21:31,590
Tell me where we're going already.

415
00:21:31,840 --> 00:21:33,380
Look!

416
00:21:33,380 --> 00:21:37,510
There's no guarantee that you won't
kill me after I tell you, right?

417
00:21:37,810 --> 00:21:39,950
I see. Uh...

418
00:21:39,950 --> 00:21:41,290
Amai.

419
00:21:41,290 --> 00:21:42,270
It's Rin Amai.

420
00:21:42,570 --> 00:21:45,100
What am I supposed to do if
you die before I get there?

421
00:21:45,100 --> 00:21:49,180
That's why! You need to! Protect me!

422
00:21:49,180 --> 00:21:50,870
And use my name already!

423
00:21:50,870 --> 00:21:52,290
Anything could happen.

424
00:21:52,290 --> 00:21:55,060
Amai, where is Higuruma?

425
00:21:55,060 --> 00:21:56,810
Well, fine.

426
00:21:56,810 --> 00:21:58,570
I'll give you a rough idea.

427
00:21:58,570 --> 00:22:01,480
The stronger people are gathered
where the city once thrived.

428
00:22:01,480 --> 00:22:03,200
Since resources are in good supply there.

429
00:22:03,200 --> 00:22:04,310
Higuruma is in...

430
00:22:03,810 --> 00:22:04,880
Higuruma is in...

431
00:22:04,880 --> 00:22:06,310
...Ikebukuro.

432
00:22:05,400 --> 00:22:06,840
...Shinjuku.

433
00:22:06,840 --> 00:22:07,680
Got it?

434
00:22:07,250 --> 00:22:07,960
Got it?

435
00:23:40,680 --> 00:23:44,430
I just sense potential
in the Culling Game.

436
00:23:44,430 --> 00:23:45,770
Every person in this nation will die.

437
00:23:45,770 --> 00:23:48,090
She deceived you.

438
00:23:48,090 --> 00:23:49,440
I'm sorry, Itadori.

439
00:23:49,440 --> 00:23:51,290
A sorcerer connected to Kenjaku?!

440
00:23:51,290 --> 00:23:52,280
I want to talk.

441
00:23:51,990 --> 00:23:55,060
Next Episode
Tokyo No. 1 Colony, Part 2

442
00:23:52,280 --> 00:23:53,980
We're having a retrial.
